		<!-- Content -->
		<div class="container"><h1>Add a Receipt</h1>
<p>Record a new purchase with its vendor, date, amount, and category.</p>

<h3>Steps</h3>
<ol>
	<li>In the <strong>Receipt List</strong> window, click <strong>Add</strong>.</li>
	<li>In the <strong>Receipt Details</strong> window, type the <strong>Vendor</strong> name, pick the <strong>Date</strong> from the calendar, and type the <strong>Amount</strong>.</li>
	<li>Choose a <strong>Category</strong>: Supplies, Meals, Travel, Utilities, Equipment, or Other.</li>
</ol>
<img src="/images/add-form.png" width="100%" alt="Receipt Details form filled in for Staples">

<ol start="4">
	<li>If the purchase counts toward your taxes, check <strong>Tax-related</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<img src="/images/add-tax-form.png" width="100%" alt="Receipt Details form with Tax-related checked">

<ol start="5">
	<li>Click <strong>Save</strong>. The receipt appears in the list, and the receipt count at the bottom goes up.</li>
</ol>
<img src="/images/receipt-list.png" width="100%" alt="Receipt List showing three receipts">

<p>If a field is missing or the amount is not a valid number, an error message appears on the form and nothing is saved until you fix it.</p>
<p>Next: <a href="/edit">edit a receipt</a>.</p>

<p>You are ready to go. Next, learn how to <a href="/add">add your first receipt</a>.</p>
